  "body": {
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "For every pair \\((A,B)\\) of normalized nonnegative \\(2\\times2\\) probability tables for which \\(F(A,B)\\ne\\varnothing\\), and every \\((c,d)\\in F(A,B)\\), the handle \\(Hthr\\) constructs a finite model \\(M\\in MC(A,B)\\) with binary-valued roots \\(U0,V0\\) (possibly degenerate), a private root \\(W0\\) with at most eight support points, mutually independent roots, and one deterministic outcome function \\(fY\\) shared by all regimes, such that \\(q=a+b-c+d\\).  The construction reproduces all four cells of \\(A\\) and all four cells of \\(B\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "A",
      "B",
      "F",
      "c",
      "d",
      "Hthr",
      "M",
      "MC",
      "U0",
      "V0",
      "W0",
      "fY",
      "q",
      "a",
      "b"
    ],
    "justification": "The common threshold construction proves that every feasible mass pair, including those on structural-zero faces, lifts without coupling the two source roots.",
    "gap": "Generic finite canonicalization does not itself provide this eight-point source-preserving certificate or its explicit zero-denominator branches.",
    "consumer": "The theorem supplies common-SCM attainment for compatibility, sharpness, exact endpoint certificates, and the fixed-graph analytic dispatch.",
    "id": "thm:resolve-b2d9584a442bdc01be2b",
